eld/id #uuid "6cc34ef4-7501-5243-a024-415bb88fbe79" :answer-field/key "The product $AC$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc01dbd0-f7a2-50df-b1f3-057f34f1bf86" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 4 & 8 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 8 & -8 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 6 & -7 & -5 \\\\ -7 & -1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, $B$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{4\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{A}_{2\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{C}_{3\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $B$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe product $BC$ is well defined. The products $BA$ and $AC$ are undefined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141a71b8-c81b-53b9-bf35-2d5da0e457ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634807} {:answer/id #uuid "48717be4-a4b7-5bb6-98f9-ad274573bee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48717be4-a4b7-5bb6-98f9-ad274573bee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634810} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bf9bf4c-2c54-5c18-9af7-933317ba12f9" :answer-field/key "The product $PR$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b09b734-cb86-5213-9db7-1cbb74225457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634809} {:answer/id #uuid "66d8091e-4749-54e4-8585-ab1faf1f4ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b09b734-cb86-5213-9db7-1cbb74225457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634809} :answer-field/id #uuid "13cdbde3-08bd-59ba-a3f9-fb5a72369788" :answer-field/key "The product $PS$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce4e31e9-705a-50a8-aeeb-199983acdbed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634813} {:answer/id #uuid "d06cef31-7f5e-5321-aa7f-6cc14fcdc5ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce4e31e9-705a-50a8-aeeb-199983acdbed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634813} :answer-field/id #uuid "99af46e7-e1ff-5a86-9292-2b7b4f47b827" :answer-field/key "The product $RS$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b043b81-1ada-5815-850e-33b61f29ebfb" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 8 & -8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, $R$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, and $S$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $R$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $RS$ and $PS$ are well defined. The product $PR$ is undefined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fab5c88-be88-5b2b-951e-75649b669262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637707} {:answer/id #uuid "57d20d35-461b-50da-80bf-22bfed6688d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fab5c88-be88-5b2b-951e-75649b669262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637707} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e5f044-8e15-5f28-be89-896a57b58f3e" :answer-field/key "$-7x-6=-7x-6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637704} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97824417-5e41-5d14-9c42-4dcc3961bb90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637728} {:answer/id #uuid "c49900be-89d8-574f-bca1-f6e610489006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c49900be-89d8-574f-bca1-f6e610489006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637735} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d6f188f-5c73-59ff-97fb-43bbe28343e9" :answer-field/key "$4x-3=5x-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637714} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f670177-a7c2-51db-8f6c-78087617c0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637720} {:answer/id #uuid "94c88f2e-e807-5071-be0e-b85832b68b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f670177-a7c2-51db-8f6c-78087617c0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637720} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ec1c57a-e163-5f37-a4c7-57e3f4345d1d" :answer-field/key "$-3x+1=-3x+6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03b3170c-3ed8-5ab0-842f-228de8b151e6" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7x-6 & =-7x-6 \\\\ -7x-6+7x & =-7x-6+7x \\\\ -6 & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-7x-6=-7x-6$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3 & =5x-1 \\\\ 4x-3-4x & =5x-1-4x \\\\ -3 & =x-1 \\\\ -3+1 & =x-1+1 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $4x-3=5x-1$ has the unique solution $x=-2.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+1 & =-3x+6 \\\\ -3x+1+3x & =-3x+6+3x \\\\ 1 & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-7x-6=-7x-6$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "078b4a28-afdf-5b02-99d0-b56048c69026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637697} {:answer/id #uuid "8bef825f-15ba-5843-af77-5b733c5c56d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "078b4a28-afdf-5b02-99d0-b56048c69026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637697} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b271c2c-039e-5d02-b5ba-674484523026" :answer-field/key "$4x-9=3x-9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637711} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "260b1c68-e480-5ebf-adef-fc544f810380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637701} {:answer/id #uuid "42daa6df-03a7-5201-ab2d-a080be565a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42daa6df-03a7-5201-ab2d-a080be565a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637706} :answer-field/id #uuid "858916b2-c8c0-5178-877c-78739f7d3bfb" :answer-field/key "$-3x+7=-4x+7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d57565a-352b-53c5-ad05-952578adc3c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637705} {:answer/id #uuid "77cd05b4-ce77-5e41-ae9c-00fbe7f10505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d57565a-352b-53c5-ad05-952578adc3c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637705} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbf11801-831c-562f-ab69-16accef7e23a" :answer-field/key "$x+1=x+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32e0d046-d5da-5e0d-b3f6-0971ff276caa" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =x+1 \\\\ x+1-x & =x+1-x \\\\ 1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $x+1=x+1$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-9 & =3x-9 \\\\ 4x-9-3x & =3x-9-3x \\\\ x-9 & =-9 \\\\ x-9+9 & =-9+9 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $4x-9=3x-9$ has the unique solution $x=0.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+7 & =-4x+7 \\\\ -3x+7+4x & =-4x+7+4x \\\\ x+7 & =7 \\\\ x+7-7 & =7-7 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-3x+7=-4x+7$ has the unique solution $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x+1=x+1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19c3b30f-4846-5229-b821-012fb68d546a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637699} {:answer/id #uuid "8d933712-5fe6-5fa7-a3d4-4e5b0c226879" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d933712-5fe6-5fa7-a3d4-4e5b0c226879" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637724} :answer-field/id #uuid "62c58814-98b4-5a44-9177-09c8a7c6623c" :answer-field/key "$2x+6=2x-9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bdb81b9-cee5-5e38-8d41-716a1343c60f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637729} {:answer/id #uuid "9db9e3cc-3161-5c68-923d-e4cb0d1c838f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bdb81b9-cee5-5e38-8d41-716a1343c60f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637729} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dcf7adb-4b71-5b06-9530-82b553a5e1d0" :answer-field/key "$-4x+9=-4x+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "930b0792-c12b-599e-8baf-7c40b9b60222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637725} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e4ec73-d9e8-58fc-875c-52c8586061b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4e4ec73-d9e8-58fc-875c-52c8586061b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637737} :answer-field/id #uuid "b58d460d-b6f1-58b7-a647-8905bcac9102" :answer-field/key "$-x+7=-x+7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "560d42c5-e95c-5f3e-aca7-05cab35fcee0" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+7 & =-x+7 \\\\ -x+7+x & =-x+7+x \\\\ 7 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-x+7=-x+7$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+9 & =-4x+1 \\\\ -4x+9+4x & =-4x+1+4x \\\\ 9 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+6 & =2x-9 \\\\ 2x+6-2x & =2x-9-2x \\\\ 6 & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-x+7=-x+7$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81472a83-0332-5918-a96e-fe5ca570d4c6" :