86c8-d3d8-579a-be2e-7d5b74e41b83" :answer-field/key "$2x+9=2x+9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4c73443-b9e7-5150-a02a-0a4899b0c0d2" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+9 & =2x+9 \\\\ 2x+9-2x & =2x+9-2x \\\\ 9 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $2x+9=2x+9$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+9 & =3x+9 \\\\ 3x+9-3x & =3x+9-3x \\\\ 9 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $3x+9=3x+9$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-2 & =2x-4 \\\\ 2x-2-2x & =2x-4-2x \\\\ -2 & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2x+9=2x+9$; $3x+9=3x+9$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186638394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124477 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8305b6d8-1288-5a32-9225-aead2c8eb577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638415} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7d22a4-53fc-5f33-bd6c-5633d31be343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8305b6d8-1288-5a32-9225-aead2c8eb577" :ans